# Spojex: push every change

After finishing a fix or feature in any Spojex repo (`spojex_admin`, `spojex_backend`, `spojext_superapp`), **commit and push to GitHub without waiting for the user to ask**. These repos deploy automatically from `main`.

- Do not ask “should I push?” — push as part of finishing the work.
- Use a concise commit message focused on why.
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, private keys).
- Prefer `required_permissions: ["all"]` for git write/push outside the workspace sandbox.
- If push fails, fix auth/permissions and retry; report the PR/commit URL or `git log -1` hash when done.
